# =============================================================================
# WHITELIST-STYLE .gitignore
#
# Everything is ignored by default. Only paths explicitly re-included below can
# be tracked. Anything generated from or copied out of RimWorld is treated as
# private/local unless explicitly proven safe to publish.
#
# Before adding a new top-level entry here, ask: could a game file, a decompiler
# output, or a dump ever end up inside it? If yes, do not whitelist it.
#
# The pre-commit hook (tools/git-hooks/pre-commit) is the second line of
# defence; see docs/provenance.md.
# =============================================================================

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry (this covers RimWorld/, local/, target/, ...)
/*

# 2. Re-include the project skeleton
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE-MIT
!/LICENSE-APACHE
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/config.example.toml
!/rustfmt.toml
!/crates/
!/docs/
!/tests/
!/tools/

# Explicitly local-only (already covered by `/*`; listed for clarity).
/target/
/local/
/research_queue/
/saves/
/RimWorld/

# 3. Inside whitelisted directories, block anything that looks like game
#    content, decompiler output, dumps, binaries or build products.
target/
**/research_queue/
**/traces/
**/probe*/
**/saves/
**/screenshots/
**/local/
**/research/
**/game/
**/decompiled/
**/RimWorld/
**/Data/Core/
**/Defs/

# Executables, libraries, debug info
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.so
*.dylib
*.mdb
*.il

# Unity / game data containers
*.assets
*.resS
*.resource
*.bundle
*.unity3d
globalgamemanagers*
level[0-9]*

# Decompiler projects / output / C# sources
*.cs
*.csproj
*.sln
*.ilspy*
*.dnspy*
*.dotpeek*

# Dumps
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*.dump
*.core

# Textures, images, audio, fonts
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.dds
*.psd
*.tga
*.bmp
*.gif
*.webp
*.ogg
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.ttf
*.otf
*.fnt

# XML (RimWorld Defs/Languages are XML). Only synthetic test fixtures allowed.
*.xml

# Archives (RimWorld ships language packs as .tar)
*.tar
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz

# Logs, traces, crash output
*.log
*.trace
*.etl
*.crash

# Local configuration (contains a machine-specific install path)
config.toml
*.local.toml
.env

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# 4. Narrow, explicit exceptions
#    Synthetic XML fixtures written by hand for this project. Each must carry
#    the marker comment `synthetic-fixture` (enforced by the pre-commit hook).
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.xml
!/crates/*/tests/fixtures/**/*.xml
#    Our own screenshots / diagrams for documentation. Review every image by
#    hand: screenshots must not be used to redistribute game textures.
!/docs/images/*.png
